      "annotatedSteps": [
        {
          "stepNumber": 1,
          "part": null,
          "description": "Entire solution provided by student",
          "studentWork": "Let the speed of the train be x km/h. Reduced speed = (x − 8) km/h.\nTime at usual speed = 480/x, time at reduced speed = 480/(x − 8).\n480/x − 480/(x − 8) = 3\n⇒ 480(x − 8) − 480x = 3x(x − 8)\n⇒ −3840 = 3x² − 24x\n⇒ 3x² − 24x + 3840 = 0\n⇒ x² − 8x + 1280 = 0\n⇒ (x − 40)(x + 32) = 0\n⇒ x = 40 or x = −32. Speed cannot be negative.\n∴ Speed of the train = 40 km/h.",
