          "marksAvailable": 5.0,
          "marksAwarded": 0.0,
          "marksDeducted": 5.0,
          "teacherAnnotation": "× Work answers a different question (train speed word problem) instead of the given AP question",
          "mistakeType": "conceptual",
          "correctedWorking": "Let the first term be a and the common difference be d. Then a_1 = a and a_8 = a + 7d. Given a + (a + 7d) = 32 ⇒ 2a + 7d = 32 and a(a + 7d) = 60. From the sum, a + 7d = 32 - a. Substitute into the product: a(32 - a) = 60 ⇒ a² - 32a + 60 = 0 ⇒ (a - 30)(a - 2) = 0. Case 1: If a = 2, then 2 + 7d = 30 ⇒ d = 4. S_20 = 20/2 [2(2) + 19(4)] = 10[4 + 76] = 800. Case 2: If a = 30, then 30 + 7d = 2 ⇒ d = -4. S_20 = 20/2 [2(30) + 19(-4)] = 10[60 - 76] = -160.",
